# CoachLink Cursor Rules

## Language
- Always respond in Chinese-simplified.

## Preflight (before coding)
- Read `docs/done/engineering/PROMPT.md` first.
- Identify affected chain before edits: page/component -> service -> api -> db.
- If requirement is ambiguous, inspect code first; do not guess and modify blindly.

## Data consistency gate (high frequency regressions)
- Keep index semantics explicit and consistent in one edit chain:
  - `dayIndex`: business index (usually 1-based)
  - `arrayIndex`: array offset (0-based)
- Keep empty-value semantics consistent across layers: `null` vs `undefined` vs `''`.
- For list-edit CRUD flows, verify add/delete/update all work after changes.

## Boundary and security gate
- Frontend must not access database directly; use `@/app/service` -> `@/app/api`.
- Identity and permission must come from session, not user-provided IDs.
- Coach/student boundary checks are mandatory in related APIs.

## Recurring bug knowledge capture (team default)
- Do not rely on personal judgment only. Use the following triggers.
- When any trigger is met, you MUST append/update docs:
  1) Same bug pattern appears at least 2 times in different files/modules; or
  2) A bug belongs to known high-risk classes: index mismatch, async state/persistence mismatch, null/undefined semantics mismatch, permission/session boundary mismatch; or
  3) The fix involves behavior regression risk in CRUD/list-edit flows.

## Where to update
- Pattern-level knowledge -> append to `docs/done/engineering/高频复发Bug清单.md`.
- Checkable guardrails -> append checklist items/examples to `docs/done/engineering/代码检查清单.md`.
- If coding conventions change, add a short pointer in `docs/done/engineering/PROMPT.md`.

## Append format (keep short)
- For `高频复发Bug清单.md`, append one compact block:
  - 现象
  - 根因
  - 统一规则
  - 改动前自检
- For `代码检查清单.md`, append:
  - 一个“错误示例 vs 正确示例”
  - 一个可勾选检查项

## Constraints
- Do not create long new markdown files unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer appending to existing docs instead of creating new docs.
- Keep each new rule minimal and actionable.
- Never revert unrelated user changes.
- Never use destructive git commands unless explicitly requested.

## Done criteria (must pass before final reply)
- Run lints for edited files and fix newly introduced issues when feasible.
- Ensure key path works for this change (especially CRUD/list-edit operations).
- In final reply, include:
  - `是否触发知识沉淀：是/否`
  - `若是，已更新文件：...`

